<title>USA: Brazil's Banco ABC-ROMA SA unit sets $30 mln Euro.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Banco ABC-ROMA SA unit sets $30 mln Euro.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following Eurobond issue from ABC-ROMA Banking Ltd, a wholly-owned subsidiary of Brazil's Banco ABC-ROMA SA, was launched and priced on Thursday, according to lead manager Credit Lyonnais.</p>
<p>ABC-ROMA Banking is based in Nassau, Bahamas.</p>
<p>BORROWER ABC-ROMA BANKING LTD</p>
<p>AMT $30 MLN	  COUPON 8.00 PCT    MATURITY 3/13/1998</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.76466 FIRST PAY DATE 9/13/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S NR    YIELD 8.25 PCT     PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P NR				   CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672</p>
</text>
